---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Split from '../components/Split.astro';
import NoteBox from '../components/NoteBox.astro';
import ReserveCTA from '../components/ReserveCTA.astro';
import ReserveContactBlock from '../components/ReserveContactBlock.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business';
import { img } from '../lib/images';

const heroImage = img('farm/property_overview.jpg');
const ogImage = await getImage({ src: heroImage, width: 1200, format: 'webp' });
---

<PageLayout
  title="FAQs & Contact — Wild on the Farm | Boquete Cloud Forest Lodge"
  description="Answers to common questions about staying at Wild on the Farm, Boquete Cloud Forest Lodge, and how to reach us directly."
  path="/faqs-contact/"
  image={ogImage.src}
  pullIntro="Everything guests tend to ask before arriving — and if it's not here, just write to us directly."
>
  <Fragment slot="hero">
    <PageHero image={heroImage} alt="Aerial view of the farm property" eyebrow="Plan Your Stay">
      Questions, answered. And how to reach us.
    </PageHero>
  </Fragment>

  <Section noPadTop label="Get In Touch" heading="We answer WhatsApp faster than email.">
    <div class="contact-list contact-list-lg">
      <a href={business.whatsappHref}>{business.phone} (WhatsApp)</a>
      <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section bg="cream" label="Frequently Asked Questions" heading="Before you book.">
    <Split>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How do I get to the farm?</h3>
        <p>
          The last kilometre of the road is very steep and requires a 4x4. If you're arriving in a
          regular car, park at the bottom and we'll come get you. If you arrive on foot, we'll
          pick you up and drop you back in Boquete (5 km away) at the end of your stay. If you'd
          like to go into Boquete during your stay, you can book a 4x4 taxi for $25 — or, whenever
          we're heading into town ourselves, you're welcome to ride along with us for free.
          Traveling from further afield? See our full guide on{' '}
          <a href="/journal/boquete-travel-guide/">getting to Boquete from Panama City</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Is there Wi-Fi?</h3>
        <p>
          By design, there's no Wi-Fi or TV inside the cabins — the silence is part of the
          experience. Wi-Fi is available in the common areas for anyone who needs to check in with
          the outside world.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Split>

    <div class="faq-item max-prose">
      <h3>What about electricity — can I bring a hairdryer?</h3>
      <p>
        We're entirely off-grid and generate our own solar power, so high-draw resistance
        appliances like hairdryers aren't permitted. There's no shortage of power otherwise — we
        just ask every guest to use only the lights they need, switch off what isn't in use, and
        remember to turn off the bathroom light when you leave.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Split>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What's the weather like?</h3>
        <p>
          Pleasant, thanks to the altitude — you escape the heavy, unbearable heat found lower
          down. Pack a fleece, a light rain jacket, and hiking boots if you plan on walking the
          trails.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Will I definitely see the Quetzal, or the jaguar?</h3>
        <p>
          The best window for birdwatching — and for Quetzal sightings especially — is between
          March 15 and May 15, when most birds are nesting and Quetzals are abundant in the area.
          Outside that window sightings are still possible, just less reliable. Rarer sightings
          like the jaguar are genuinely rare, even here — this is a working cloud forest, not a
          zoo.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Split>

    <Split>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Is a guide required for hiking?</h3>
        <p>
          Some sections are walkable without a guide if you're an experienced hiker comfortable
          navigating on your own. For hikes over 3 hours into the cloud forest, a guide is
          strongly recommended — the trails from the farm are faint and remote — though
          experienced hikers who want their independence are free to go without one. All hikers
          are asked to sign a liability waiver beforehand, and guests should have their own travel
          or personal insurance.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do you accommodate dietary restrictions?</h3>
        <p>Just let us know if you have a special diet or any allergies when you book, and we'll plan meals around it.</p>
      </div>
    </Split>

    <Split>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What are meals like?</h3>
        <p>
          Breakfast is included and generally hearty, served between 8 and 9am. Dinner can be
          reserved each evening — two appetizers, a main dish, and a dessert. We bake our own
          bread.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Are pets welcome?</h3>
        <p>We're sorry, but we don't accept pets. We keep animals on the farm, and outside animals cause them a great deal of stress.</p>
      </div>
    </Split>

    <Split>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Are children welcome?</h3>
        <p>For safety reasons, children under 12 aren't accepted, and there are no extra beds available in the cabins.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What's your cancellation policy?</h3>
        <p>
          Free cancellation up to 1 month before arrival. From 1 month to 15 days out, 50% is
          refundable; from 15 days to 1 week out, 25% is refundable. Inside 1 week of arrival,
          bookings are non-refundable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Split>

    <Split>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How do I book?</h3>
        <p>
          Reach out directly by WhatsApp or email — tell us your dates and what you're hoping to
          experience, and we'll help you pick the right cabin and plan the stay.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What payment methods do you accept?</h3>
        <NoteBox variant="todo">
          <p>
            Accepted payment methods not yet decided — cash, transfer, card, deposit vs. balance
            on arrival, etc.
          </p>
        </NoteBox>
      </div>
    </Split>

    <div class="faq-item max-prose">
      <h3>Any apps you'd recommend bringing?</h3>
      <p>
        For birdwatching, we recommend downloading (and updating) the Merlin Bird ID app before
        you arrive — it's a great help identifying what you're seeing. If you're into plants and
        flowers, a specialized plant-identification app is useful too for putting a name to what's
        growing around you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <ReserveCTA>
    <Fragment slot="left">
      <div class="section-label">Still Have Questions?</div>
      <h2>We're happy to talk it through.</h2>
      <p>Write to us directly and we'll help you plan your stay, whatever's still unclear.</p>
      <div class="contact-list">
        <a href="/rates-retreats/">Rates &amp; Retreats →</a>
        <a href="/stay/">See The Cabins →</a>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="right">
      <ReserveContactBlock />
    </Fragment>
  </ReserveCTA>
</PageLayout>
